{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-444e6904-b161-413b-8369-d8cda8085c7f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93824b3f238c5271","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9019-7klxbe38/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9019-E001.md","content":"# Tutorial packaging format: metadata, pinned images, and validation manifest\n\n## Description\n\nDefines the packaging format that makes each tutorial a versioned, independently\ntestable artifact: a metadata description of the tutorial, pinned references to\nthe images it runs against, and a validation manifest capturing how the tutorial\nis certified against a platform release. The format is the contract between\nauthored tutorial content and the Dashboard gallery that launches it, so\ntutorials can be added, versioned, and validated without Dashboard releases.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define the tutorial metadata that describes a packaged tutorial (identity,\n  core journey, presentation information) and is consumable by the tutorial\n  gallery\n- Define the image-pinning rules: each packaged tutorial records the exact\n  image references (workbench image and any other images it requires) it runs\n  against\n- Define the validation manifest: the checks a tutorial must pass to be\n  certified against a given platform release\n- Provide the validation tooling that executes a packaged tutorial's validation\n  manifest and reports pass/fail results\n- Deliver the format as a documented specification together with one reference\n  tutorial packaged in the format\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The packaging format specification defines all three constituents stated in\n  the strategy: metadata, pinned images, and a validation manifest\n- The reference tutorial is packaged in the format and its validation manifest\n  executes via the validation tooling with a deterministic pass/fail result\n- Every image reference in a packaged tutorial is pinned to an exact reference\n  at packaging time\n- Packaging and validating a new or updated tutorial requires no change to the\n  Dashboard — tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard\n  releases\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-3 (P1) — full coverage: the tutorial packaging format, its metadata,\n  pinned images, and validation manifest, enabling versioned and independently\n  testable tutorials\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":35347,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a09083951618bd4b","agent_id":"a22aa6835961655f2","session_id":"8fde49e5-4b3d-4b7f-9888-7a2f9f5128eb","uuid":"65ca2826-c7a2-41e3-93a8-4cf364756561","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:26:30.951Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019"}
