 on the Data Science Pipelines surface. |\n65\t| HLR-2 — six curated, release-tested tutorials | P0 | E002, E004 | E002 authors and tests all six; E004 provides the Data Science Pipelines team's validation of the pipeline tutorials against the current release. |\n66\t| HLR-3 — tutorial packaging format | P1 | E001 | Epic is P0 by priority inheritance: it blocks both P0 epics (E002, E003). |\n67\t| HLR-4 — gallery usage and contribution documentation | P2 | E005 | docs-authoring epic; priority P1 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1), exempt from priority inheritance. |\n68\t\n69\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n70\t\n71\t## Health Warnings\n72\t\n73\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted Teams\n74\t  table, no per-component change descriptions (Affected Components is a bare\n75\t  list), no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n76\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were derived from\n77\t  `.context/architecture-context/` owning teams; acceptance criteria were derived\n78\t  from the HLRs.\n79\t- **Team assumptions:** tutorial authoring and the packaging format are assigned\n80\t  to the Workbenches team (owning team of the Notebooks component per\n81\t  `notebooks.md`). If a dedicated enablement/content team owns tutorial\n82\t  authoring, reassign E001/E002. The documentation epic is assigned to a docs\n83\t  team (\"RHOAI Docs\"); the strategy names no docs team and no architecture\n84\t  context file exists for the Documentation component.\n85\t- **Passive component classification:** Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines are\n86\t  treated as passive (no code changes indicated; the launch mechanics use\n87\t  existing Notebook and KFP v2 surfaces). Workbench launch validation is folded\n88\t  into acceptance criteria on E002/E003 (same owning team as Notebooks content).\n89\t  The Data Science Pipelines validation became a separate epic (E004) because a\n90\t  different team owns that surface.\n91\t- **Out-of-scope consistency:** contribution tooling is out of scope while HLR-4\n92\t  asks only for contribution *documentation* — consistent, not a scope trap.\n93\t  Submission tooling must not creep into E005's scope.\n94\t- **Priority note:** HLR-3 is P1 but E001 is P0 by inheritance (an epic blocking\n95\t  all P0 work is implicitly P0). Not an inversion — it reflects the enablement\n96\t  chain.\n97\t\n98\t## Tiered Delivery\n99\t\n100\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all components\n101\tare in the platform (architecture context files exist for Dashboard, Notebooks,\n102\tand Data Science Pipelines; all are Konflux-onboarded GA components).\n103\t\n104\t## Component Mapping Notes\n105\t\n106\t- E001/E002 carry component `Notebooks` (canonical list) as the single\n107\t  most-relevant name, although the six tutorials span workbench, data prep,\n108\t  training, pipeline, deployment, and RAG journeys (pipeline surface belongs to\n109\t  Data Science Pipelines, deployment to serving components). The span is noted\n110\t  here rather than fragmenting the content-authoring epic across components.\n111\t- E003 → `Dashboard`, E004 → `Data Science Pipelines`, E005 → `Documentation`,\n112\t  all verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n113\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-849adb4e23a63a73","agent_id":"a6018b7a821d5d3b3","session_id":"8fde49e5-4b3d-4b7f-9888-7a2f9f5128eb","uuid":"41a80e58-994a-4b14-ab5d-b5a84f3b36fe","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:32:15.284Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b14d1bcbeb45a156","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
