{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6fa7aa00bb744a2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 4\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\tThe strategy explicitly spans three kinds of work with different owners and review\n13\tprocesses: product code (the Dashboard gallery and launch mechanics), authored\n14\tcontent (the six curated tutorials), and documentation. It is therefore not\n15\tbelow-threshold and not docs-only; it proceeds through full decomposition.\n16\t\n17\t## Epic List\n18\t\n19\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n20\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n21\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format: metadata, pinned images, and validation manifest | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n22\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Author and test six curated getting-started tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Dashboard tutorial gallery with one-click launch into projects | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Validate tutorial pipeline import and execution on Data Science Pipelines | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Document tutorial gallery usage and the tutorial contribution process | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Docs | P1 |\n26\t\n27\t## Dependency DAG\n28\t\n29\t```mermaid\n30\tgraph TD\n31\t  E001[RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 packaging format] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 six tutorials]\n32\t  E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 gallery and launch]\n33\t  E002 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 pipeline validation]\n34\t  E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 documentation]\n35\t  E002 --> E005\n36\t  E003 --> E005\n37\t  E004 --> E005\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t## DAG Justification\n41\t\n42\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n43\t|------|------|-----------|\n44\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Tutorials are authored, packaged, and validated in the packaging format; content authoring builds against the format definition. |\n45\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (artifact another epic's code builds against) | The gallery renders tutorial metadata and launches pinned images; its code builds against the format, which must exist first. |\n46\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12 (consumer of authored artifact) | Pipeline-tutorial validation consumes the authored, packaged pipeline tutorials; it cannot start before they exist. |\n47\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the contribution process, which is defined by the packaging format. |\n48\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation references the curated tutorial set. |\n49\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the implemented gallery behavior. |\n50\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation's validation-requirements section reflects the validated pipeline path. |\n51\t\n52\t**Deliberately absent edges:**\n53\t- E002 ∥ E003 (Rules 14/15): tutorial authoring and gallery implementation are\n54\t  different repos/surfaces with no shared build artifact beyond the packaging\n55\t  format (both gated on E001). The end-to-end \"launch a tutorial from the\n56\t  gallery\" check is an acceptance criterion on the gallery epic, exercised at\n57\t  execution time once a packaged tutorial exists — not a DAG edge.\n58\t- E003 ∥ E004: the Data Science Pipelines validation runs against the packaged\n59\t  pipeline tutorials directly and does not need the gallery UI.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n62\t\n63\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n64\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n65\t| HLR-1 — tutorial gallery with one-click launch into project | P0 | E003, E004 | E003 delivers the gallery and launch mechanics; E004 validates the pipeline-import launch path on the Data Science Pipelines surface. |\n66\t| HLR-2 — six curated, release-tested tutorials | P0 | E002, E004 | E002 authors and tests all six; E004 provides the Data Science Pipelines team's validation of the pipeline tutorials against the current release. |\n67\t| HLR-3 — tutorial packaging format | P1 | E001 | Epic is P0 by priority inheritance: it blocks both P0 epics (E002, E003). |\n68\t| HLR-4 — gallery usage and contribution documentation | P2 | E005 | docs-authoring epic; priority P1 per the docs-authoring exception (strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1), exempt from priority inheritance. |\n69\t\n70\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n71\t\n72\t## Health Warnings\n73\t\n74\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted Teams\n75\t  table, no per-component change descriptions (Affected Components is a bare\n76\t  list), no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no\n77\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were derived from\n78\t  `.context/architecture-context/` owning teams; acceptance criteria were derived\n79\t  from the HLRs.\n80\t- **Team assumptions:** tutorial authoring and the packaging format are assigned\n81\t  to the Workbenches team (owning team of the Notebooks component per\n82\t  `notebooks.md`). If a dedicated enablement/content team owns tutorial\n83\t  authoring, reassign E001/E002. The documentation epic is assigned to a docs\n84\t  team (\"RHOAI Docs\"); the strategy names no docs team and no architecture\n85\t  context file exists for the Documentation component.\n86\t- **Passive component classification:** Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines are\n87\t  treated as passive (no code changes indicated; the launch mechanics use\n88\t  existing Notebook and KFP v2 surfaces). Workbench launch validation is folded\n89\t  into acceptance criteria on E002/E003 (same owning team as Notebooks content).\n90\t  The Data Science Pipelines validation became a separate epic (E004) because a\n91\t  different team owns that surface.\n92\t- **Out-of-scope consistency:** contribution tooling is out of scope while HLR-4\n93\t  asks only for contribution *documentation* — consistent, not a scope trap.\n94\t  Submission tooling must not creep into E005's scope.\n95\t- **Priority note:** HLR-3 is P1 but E001 is P0 by inheritance (an epic blocking\n96\t  all P0 work is implicitly P0). Not an inversion — it reflects the enablement\n97\t  chain.\n98\t- **E002 size (above guideline, not split):** estimated at ~3 weeks of a single\n99\t  author's effort (six heterogeneous journeys across two content formats),\n100\t  above the ~2-week guideline. Not split because it is one logical change — a\n101\t  single homogeneous content-authoring sweep sharing one packaging/validation\n102\t  pipeline and one release-certification loop; splitting by journey count or by\n103\t  work type (authoring vs packaging vs testing) would duplicate the shared\n104\t  setup and fragment the format's single validation loop. Conditional re-split\n105\t  trigger: if, once the first two tutorials are authored and validated, more\n106\t  than one week of estimated effort remains for the other four — or if\n107\t  separate authors are assigned per journey family — split E002 along the\n108\t  notebook-journeys vs pipeline-journeys axis into parallel epics.\n109\t- **E001 reference tutorial is a minimal exemplar:** E001 deliberately bundles\n110\t  one reference tutorial with the format spec and validation tooling — it\n111\t  exists solely as the format's test fixture and must stay a minimal exemplar;\n112\t  it must not grow into substantive tutorial content that shadows the\n113\t  content-authoring deliverable (E002), which owns the six curated tutorials.\n114\t\n115\t## Tiered Delivery\n116\t\n117\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all components\n118\tare in the platform (architecture context files exist for Dashboard, Notebooks,\n119\tand Data Science Pipelines; all are Konflux-onboarded GA components).\n120\t\n121\t## Component Mapping Notes\n122\t\n123\t- E001/E002 carry component `Notebooks` (canonical list) as the single\n124\t  most-relevant name, although the six tutorials span workbench, data prep,\n125\t  training, pipeline, deployment, and RAG journeys (pipeline surface belongs to\n126\t  Data Science Pipelines, deployment to serving components). The span is noted\n127\t  here rather than fragmenting the content-authoring epic across components.\n128\t- E003 → `Dashboard`, E004 → `Data Science Pipelines`, E005 → `Documentation`,\n129\t  all verbatim from `.context/rhai-components.txt`.\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b46dd6bfafb29f3c","agent_id":"a44a4cee62a9037ef","session_id":"8fde49e5-4b3d-4b7f-9888-7a2f9f5128eb","uuid":"170d5366-a4e7-4d31-90bc-a4150872c03e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:33:22.277Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6fa7aa00bb744a2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
