{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac2fa644cd480bb6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: 'Tutorial packaging format: metadata, pinned images, and validation manifest'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 0\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 0\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: 1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format: metadata, pinned images, and validation manifest\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDefines the packaging format that makes each tutorial a versioned, independently\n34\ttestable artifact: a metadata description of the tutorial, pinned references to\n35\tthe images it runs against, and a validation manifest capturing how the tutorial\n36\tis certified against a platform release. The format is the contract between\n37\tauthored tutorial content and the Dashboard gallery that launches it, so\n38\ttutorials can be added, versioned, and validated without Dashboard releases.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define the tutorial metadata that describes a packaged tutorial (identity,\n43\t  core journey, presentation information) and is consumable by the tutorial\n44\t  gallery\n45\t- Define the image-pinning rules: each packaged tutorial records the exact\n46\t  image references (workbench image and any other images it requires) it runs\n47\t  against\n48\t- Define the validation manifest: the checks a tutorial must pass to be\n49\t  certified against a given platform release\n50\t- Provide the validation tooling that executes a packaged tutorial's validation\n51\t  manifest and reports pass/fail results\n52\t- Deliver the format as a documented specification together with one reference\n53\t  tutorial packaged in the format. The reference tutorial is a minimal exemplar\n54\t  that serves as the format's test fixture only — it is not a curated tutorial\n55\t  and must not grow into substantive content; authoring the curated tutorial\n56\t  set is a separate content-authoring deliverable outside this epic\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- The packaging format specification defines all three constituents stated in\n61\t  the strategy: metadata, pinned images, and a validation manifest\n62\t- A minimal reference tutorial is packaged in the format and its validation\n63\t  manifest executes via the validation tooling with a deterministic pass/fail\n64\t  result\n65\t- Every image reference in a packaged tutorial is pinned to an exact reference\n66\t  at packaging time\n67\t- Packaging and validating a new or updated tutorial requires no change to the\n68\t  Dashboard — tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard\n69\t  releases\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- HLR-3 (P1) — full coverage: the tutorial packaging format, its metadata,\n74\t  pinned images, and validation manifest, enabling versioned and independently\n75\t  testable tutorials\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b46dd6bfafb29f3c","agent_id":"a44a4cee62a9037ef","session_id":"8fde49e5-4b3d-4b7f-9888-7a2f9f5128eb","uuid":"1d56ce0f-7919-46ad-ba55-b862b9068ff1","timestamp":"2026-10-26T16:33:25.808Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac2fa644cd480bb6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review revised decomposition"}
